From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:05:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gugu: keep confirmed context windows across adapter processes

Why: until a turn's `result.modelUsage` confirms it, a session's context
window is guessed from the model's name ("1m" in the id or description, else
200000). Opus 5.5 under Claude Code 2.1.282 has a native 1M window and ids
without "1m" (`opus`, `claude-opus-5-5`), so every first turn streams
`size: 200000` and only the result corrects it to 1M. The bridge already
learns the confirmed window, but only in process memory; Gugu runs one adapter
process per session, so every session (and every runtime fork) starts with an
empty cache and shows the guess (gugu#6552). No cheap source of the real
window exists before the first result: initialize, supportedModels,
getSettings, getStatus and system/init do not carry it, and getContextUsage
holds every other control request (setModel waited 5.6-14.2 s behind it).

This patch
- keeps the confirmed windows in `$CLAUDE_AGENT_ACP_STATE_DIR/context-windows.json`
  when the client names that directory (unset: nothing is read or written,
  the cache stays per-process as upstream). Only SHA-256 hashes of the cache
  keys are stored, because the keys embed credential env values; logout
  clears the file with the in-memory cache;
- marks a `usage_update` whose `size` is still the unconfirmed guess with
  `_meta["_claude/contextWindowEstimated"]: true`, so a client does not show a
  guess as the session's limit (ACP requires `size` to be a number).

Upstream: none yet. The in-process cache it extends is upstream's fix for
#596; this only lets the confirmed windows outlive the process.

Drop when: upstream persists confirmed windows itself, or Claude reports a
session's context window before its first turn cheaply.
